  "description": "A shared-nothing io_uring runtime for .NET: one ring per reactor thread, inline completions, zero native dependencies. The engine - reactor, connection, and the IRingHost client seam. Includes TLS termination: the OpenSSL handshake driven over the ring, then kernel TLS (kTLS) transmit offload, so handlers keep writing plaintext. TLS needs OpenSSL 3 and the Linux tls module; nothing else does, and neither is loaded unless you use it.",
